%% Purpose: Proposal status lifecycle
%% Scope: TaskApplication-backed proposal state transitions
%% Excludes: Assignment rules (see act_01c), ranking (see act_02d)
%% Related: task_assignment_rules.ts:canApplyForTask, canProcessApplication

stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> pending : User sends proposal<br/>(message, portfolio_links)<br/>canApplyForTask checks:<br/>• not own task<br/>• public visibility<br/>• not assigned<br/>• not past deadline<br/>• no duplicate

    pending --> approved : Authorized task/project/organization<br/>reviewer approves<br/>→ Create TaskAssignment<br/>→ Auto-reject others
    pending --> rejected : Authorized task/project/organization<br/>reviewer rejects<br/>(with rejection_reason)
    pending --> withdrawn : Contributor withdraws<br/>(own pending only)

    approved --> [*]
    rejected --> [*]
    withdrawn --> [*]

    note right of pending
        Current command authorizes task creator,
        project owner/manager, and organization
        owner/admin through resolved context.
        ──────────────────
        Approving does NOT change task status.
        Task stays in current status.
        Assignee must manually start work.
    end note

    note left of approved
        On approval (ProcessMarketplaceApplicationCommand):
        • INSERT task_assignment (status=active)
        • SET task.assigned_to = contributor/applicant_id
        • Reject all other pending proposals
        • Audit event
        • Notify contributor
    end note
